  "id": "COMPOUND:611 - DISEASE:1454",
  "verbalization": "Efavirenz is implicated in the pathogenesis of High density lipoid deficiency through a complex network of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that efavirenz affects multiple proteins, including oxysterol binding protein like 10 and keratin associated protein 13-2, which are involved in the regulation of lipid metabolism. These proteins are linked to conditions such as myopathy secondary to selenium and vitamin E deficiency, which in turn contribute to the development of High density lipoid deficiency. The observed relationships indicate that efavirenz may disrupt normal cellular processes that maintain lipid homeostasis, potentially leading to the deficiency. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which efavirenz could influence lipid metabolism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
